 (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Governor Greg Abbott seeks re-election against state Representative Gina Hinojosa, and the race is far closer than Texas usually allows. Polling through mid-October shows Abbott ahead by only one to two points on average, with surveys from YouGov, the University of Texas and Siena at various points putting Hinojosa in front. Expert raters mostly call the race Lean Republican, though RealClearPolitics rates it a Tossup.\n\nAbbott holds enormous structural advantages: a $67 million war chest against Hinojosa's $3 million, long statewide tenure, and a state that leaned Republican by six points. Betting markets still give him roughly three-in-four odds, reflecting a tendency of Republican incumbents to outperform late polls in Texas. Hinojosa has generated favorable coverage, and the midterm environment favors Democrats, but no debate has occurred and the incumbent has largely ignored her. The race leans Republican heading into the final stretch.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1819, "margin": -4.27}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2694, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2894, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2702, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2293, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2331, "margin": -3.3}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2978, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2717, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2616, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2625, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2248, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2304, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2288, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.255, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2522, "margin": -3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2859, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.3188, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_